  "limitations": [
    "This artifact does not independently validate market archives, source completeness, signals, intraminute execution, trade fills or full marked-equity paths. Those are the separate execution audit scope.",
    "Historical retrospective transfer is not forward live evidence; 2021 precedes development and both transfer windows are trend-friendly samples from six selected surviving assets.",
    "2021 contributes 365 of 426 observation days; the 61-day second window has 38 selected completed trades. Per-symbol minimum-trade acceptance is pooled across both windows, not separately required in each window.",
    "Circular-block intervals describe the fixed choice under within-window dependence assumptions; they do not correct the project-wide adaptive search or establish stationary future expectations.",
    "Known 2022 first-half and 2026 September selected returns remain negative at base and stress; this pass does not retroactively pass the prior all-window-positive rule.",
    "Each transfer window resets capital independently. Pooled net PnL is a sum across reset accounts, not a compounded continuous return. Long-only returns and improvement against a channel baseline are not proof of alpha against a risk-matched market benchmark.",
    "The review reads stored raw results and their identities; hashes establish the reviewed bytes, not the truth of their market execution assumptions."
  ]
